~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
if not Flags.has("blacksmith.quest_offered")
	=> first_meeting
elif Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_given") and not Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_taken")
	=> axe_on_the_ground
elif Flags.has("blacksmith.axe_given")
	=> after
elif not has_rod()
	=> no_rod
elif fish_count() >= fish_price
	=> payday
else
	=> not_enough


#=============================================================================
# The first meeting: the road is shut, he knows the other way, and his price
# is three fish. Ends by setting blacksmith.quest_offered, which is also what
# unlocks the fishing hut's door.
#=============================================================================
~ first_meeting
Blacksmith: HOY! [wait=0.4]Don't just [wave]stand[/wave] there, you'll rust! [[Visitor!|A face!|Somebody new!]]
- I have to get over the ridge.
	=> road
- Just passing through. Ignore me.
	Blacksmith: PASSING THROUGH. Ha! [wait=0.5]No.
	=> road

~ road
Blacksmith: The old ridge road? Shut. Barricaded. [shake]Nobody[/shake] goes over the ridge any more.
Blacksmith: [wait=0.6]But there is another way, and exactly one man alive knows where it starts.
Blacksmith: It's me. [[I'm the man.|That was the modest version.|You can tell by the apron.]]
- Why would you help me?
	=> price
- Name your price.
	Blacksmith: NAME YOUR PRICE. Look at him, he gets it.
	=> price

~ price
Blacksmith: Three. [wait=0.5]Fish.
- Fish?
	Blacksmith: Fish! Silver, wriggling, deeply unhelpful. You've seen fish.
- That's a lot for a road.
	Blacksmith: For THE road. Eleven days I've eaten my own bread, and my own bread is [shake]a punishment[/shake].
Blacksmith: I'd catch them myself, but the river and I have an arrangement: I stay out, it doesn't drown me.
Blacksmith: There's a rod in the old fishing hut on the north shore. Its owner's long gone.
Blacksmith: Rod. River. Three fish. Then we talk about roads.
do Flags.set_flag("blacksmith.quest_offered")
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Sent for the rod but hasn't got it yet.
#=============================================================================
~ no_rod
Blacksmith: [[Still here? The hut's north. On the shore. Where the water is.|The rod is in the HUT, friend. The hut does not walk to you.|North shore. Old hut. Rod inside. I've made it as small as it goes.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Has the rod, hasn't got three fish yet. The rotating heckling, sharpened by
# how close he actually is.
#=============================================================================
~ not_enough
if fish_count() == 0
	Blacksmith: [[Nothing. That's fewer than three, in case you were unsure.|I asked for three fish and you've brought me a damp stick and an expression.|Let me count what you've brought me. [wait=0.6]Done.]]
elif fish_count() == 1
	Blacksmith: [[ONE. One is not three! Even the goat knows that.|A fish! Now the other two, which are the ones I asked about.|One down. Two to go.]]
else
	Blacksmith: [[TWO. Agonisingly two.|Two! The third one is out there RIGHT NOW being smug.|One more. ONE. Go and be stern with the river.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Payday: takes the three fish, gives up the road, and hands over the axe the
# forest is going to need.
#=============================================================================
~ payday
Blacksmith: [wait=0.4]Is that — [wave]THREE[/wave]? Give them here before one of us changes his mind!
do take_fish()
Blacksmith: [wait=0.8]Beautiful. Ugly. Beautiful and ugly.
Blacksmith: A bargain's a bargain. The way isn't over the ridge, it's [wave]under[/wave] it — a path through the deep forest, out past the closed road.
- The forest? Are you mad?
	Blacksmith: I know! I said it and I heard it.
- Sounds easy enough.
	Blacksmith: Easy enough, he says.
Blacksmith: It's grown over, mind. Not a path, a [shake]hedge with ambitions[/shake]. You'll be cutting your way in.
Blacksmith: [wait=1]Here. My spare. Rusty, but it bites well enough on the small trees.
Blacksmith: [shake]HEADS UP![/shake]
do drop_axe()
do Flags.set_flag("blacksmith.fish_paid")
Blacksmith: [wait=0.5]...I did say heads up.
- You threw an axe at me!
	Blacksmith: I threw an axe [wave]near[/wave] you. There's a whole craft to it.
- Thanks. I think.
	Blacksmith: You're welcome. Your foot was in the landing area, mind. That's on the foot.
Blacksmith: Well? Pick it up. It's not going to leap into your hand.
Blacksmith: And mind the fragile trees. They come down fast and don't care where you're standing.
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# Thrown, and still lying in the grass where it landed.
#=============================================================================
~ axe_on_the_ground
Blacksmith: [[It's on the ground. Where I threw it. Pick it [shake]up[/shake].|The axe. Down there. Bend at the knees.|I have thrown you an axe and you have elected to stand near it.]]
=> goodbye


#=============================================================================
# After the trade.
#=============================================================================
~ after
Blacksmith: [[Still got that axe? Good. Don't bring it back.|The forest. Cut in, keep going, come out past the road.|Any more fish? [wait=0.7]No? Then mind the fragile trees.]]
=> goodbye


~ goodbye
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END
